 - **Limits:** fixed observed arrivals are deliberately not rescheduled Linux execution. Conditional service envelopes include illustrative trigger cost and all response drain; they are neither FPGA measurements nor calibrated cycle-accurate simulations.
 
+### RL-124 — Minimal-top latency sweeps are serialized-word controls, not line-DRAM projections
+
+- **Status:** confirmed wrapper-source audit; matched complete controls at the lower setting; detailed transport counters pending
+- **Scope:** `cosim/black-parrot-minimal-example`, two resident/four logical contexts, one fixed ELF, 32-line side store, pipelined responder latency 40/200 and queue four
+- **Claim:** capture on/off at latency 40 gives identical cold/target-warm/source-warm/switch-only windows of 5,544/807/1,474/721 global-CSR cycles. In the target-warm trace, all seven prefix lines are complete in the side store at measured entry, but all fifty timed prefix fetches hit ordinary L1; capture is engaged and provides no unique retained-capacity benefit in this case. The minimal top drives ordinary HP0 AR from AXI-Lite with 32-bit words and ARLEN zero. Its cold 40-to-200 increase of 20,480 counts therefore cannot be interpreted as a 160-cycle whole-line DRAM increase. Full-top `bp_axi_top` instead configures complete-line AXI bursts.
+- **Evidence:** `research/resume-retention-matrix-20261120/on40/` and `off40/`; `research/demand-capture-fullcore-20261120/`; wrapper assignments in `cosim/black-parrot-minimal-example/v/top_zynq.sv` and burst configuration in `import/black-parrot-subsystems/blackparrot/v/bp_axi_top.sv`.
+- **Meaning:** matching physical side-store bytes does not guarantee extra unique lines beyond L1. Use actual burst transport with independently fixed response bandwidth before estimating realistic latency sensitivity; keep minimal-top runs as conditional functional/capacity diagnostics.
+- **Limits:** these are synthetic nonresident prefix roundtrips with equal prior warmup, not whole Linux applications or FPGA measurements. The all-demand admission policy remains different from selected-prefix retention.
+
